# @APP_NAME@

PySide6 workbench with a responsive shell, a balanced full-height workspace
page, native FluentQt components, and explicit product boundaries.

```bash
python -m venv .venv
python -m pip install -e .
python -m unittest discover -s tests
@APP_ID@
```

The app package composes dependencies. Domain and application modules remain
independent of Qt, infrastructure owns external state, and UI modules only
render application state and publish user intent.

`ui/components/workbench_shell.py` owns wide/narrow shell geometry. Replace the
sample `ui/pages/workspace_page.py` with the product's primary workflow; keep
the centered width, material gaps, and responsive rail until the approved
design direction gives a concrete reason to change them.

## Quality report

After the window builds successfully, emit the same native Inspector report as
the C++ starter:

```bash
@APP_ID@ --quality-report
```

The command prints versioned JSON and exits. It does not change the interface.
